     "line": 2,
     "text": "## ISO 19906 Benchmark and Porosity\u2013Resistance Scaling Law Validation",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 18,
     "text": "The ISO 19906 standard (Petroleum and natural gas industries \u2014 Fixed steel offshore structures in arctic and cold regions) provides empirical formulas for estimating ice loads on vertical structures. ",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 39,
     "text": "1. Comparing peak and steady-state loads with ISO 19906 predictions",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 97,
     "text": "- **Testing:** `pytest` with 15 unit tests covering ISO 19906 formulas, scaling law fitting, and DEM simulation",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 108,
     "text": "- **ISO 19906 reference** ($F_{\\text{ISO}} = 30.0$ MN) for continuous ice",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 110,
     "text": "The peak force is in excellent agreement with ISO 19906 (7% error), while the steady-state force is much lower due to the high porosity of the rubble field ($n = 0.92$).",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 112,
     "text": "### 3.2 ISO 19906 Comparison",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 114,
     "text": "Table 1 summarizes the comparison between DEM results and ISO 19906 predictions.",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 116,
     "text": "**Table 1: DEM vs ISO 19906 Load Comparison**",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 126,
     "text": "- **Peak forces** are in reasonable agreement with ISO 19906 for Cases 1 and 4 (errors < 50%)",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 127,
     "text": "- **Steady-state forces** are much lower than ISO 19906 because the standard assumes continuous ice, not rubble",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    },
    {
     "line": 159,
     "text": "The peak forces from DEM are in good agreement with ISO 19906 for Cases 1 and 4 (errors < 50%). This is physically reasonable because:",
     "counts_as_verbatim_anchor": false
    }
